  "text": "Medical Oncology | Veterinary Medical Center\nSkip to main content\nIt looks like you're using an unsupported browser\nFor the best experience please switch to a supported browser\nChrome\nSafari\nFirefox\nEdge\nOhio State nav bar\nThe Ohio State University\nBuckeyeLink\nFind People\nWebmail\nSearch Ohio State\nOSU More Action\nVeterinary Medical Center\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nLocations\nGiving\nOpen Search Menu\n'I am a' Menu with links to the OSU Veterinary Medical Center and the College of Veterinary Medicine\nI am a...\nOSU Hamburger Menu\nServices\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nClinical Trials\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nCareers\nCareers\nEmergency\nServices\nBack to Main Menu\nServices\nServices Overview\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nClinical Trials\nBack to Main Menu\nClinical Trials\nClinical Trials Overview\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nBack to Main Menu\nAbout\nAbout Overview\nCareers\nSearch Veterinary Medical Center\nSearch Site\nServices\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nClinical Trials\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nCareers\nCareers\nEmergency\nServices\nBack to Main Menu\nServices\nServices Overview\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nClinical Trials\nBack to Main Menu\nClinical Trials\nClinical Trials Overview\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nBack to Main Menu\nAbout\nAbout Overview\nCareers\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nLocations\nGiving\nEmergency\nI am a...\nToggles the 'I am a' Menu with links to the OSU Veterinary Medical Center and the College of Veterinary Medicine\nBuckeyeLink\nFind People\nWebmail\nSearch Ohio State\nBack\nServices\nMedical Oncology\nCompanion\nMedical Oncology\nThe Medical Oncology Service at Ohio State's Veterinary Medical Center provides therapy for a variety of tumor types in both large and small animal patients. With many chemotherapeutic treatment options available, the goal of our board-certified medical oncologists is to find the approach that works best for you and your pet.\nIn this section\nHours & Appointments\nCommon Tumors\nService Highlights\nWhat to Expect\nCare Team\nClinical Trials\nGive to Medical Oncology\nIn this section\nHours & Appointments\nCommon Tumors\nService Highlights\nWhat to Expect\nCare Team\nClinical Trials\nGive to Medical Oncology\nHours & Appointment Scheduling\nOur Oncology Department sees patients by appointment only.\nThe Oncology liaison is available to answer your questions or schedule an appointment\nMonday – Friday*\n,\n8:00 am – 4:30 pm\nand may be reached at\n(614) 247-0583\nor\nosuvet.oncology@osu.edu\n.\nIf you would like your pet to be seen by one of our specialists, please have your primary care veterinarian submit a referral through our rVetLink Referral Portal. Instructions on how to submit a referral through our portal can be found in the “Referring Veterinarians” section. Once we receive the referral, our liaison will contact you to schedule an appointment.\nIf your pet is experiencing a medical emergency,\nplease contact your primary care veterinarian, the nearest emergency veterinarian hospital or visit our Emergency Department 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.\n* The office is closed daily for lunch from 1:00 to 1:30 pm. If you reach us during this time, please leave a detailed voicemail and your call will be returned.\nFor emergency assistance, call (614) 292-3551. The Oncology department is closed in observance of all federal holidays.\nCommon Tumors Treated with Chemotherapy\nThe\nfollowing tumors can by treated with chemotherapy. Often surgery or radiation therapy will be recommended as part of the comprehensive treatment for the patient.\nLymphoma\nMast Cell Tumors\nCarcinomas (Thyroid, Anal Sac, etc.)\nOsteosarcoma and other bone tumors\nTransitional cell carcinoma\nMammary gland carcinoma\nMelanoma\nFibrosarcoma\nLeukemia\nOral tumors - all types\nMany other tumor types, call for more information\nService Highlights\nBoard-certified Medical Oncologists\nChemo delivery\nIn-house animal boarding\nWhat to Expect\nIf your veterinarian provides an unconfirmed diagnosis of cancer in your pet, have him or her call our hospital and discuss your pet’s case with the Medical Oncologist and to set up a consult. Your veterinarian will need to provide you with copies of your pet's records and any existing imaging (if applicable) prior to your appointment. During your appointment, the Medical Oncologist witll examine and refer to or discuss with the Integrated Oncology team to determine if any additional diagnostic imaging and testing may be warranted. If additional imaging and testing are necessary, your Medical Oncologist will provide the details and discuss available treatment options. Your pet may also qualify for one our\nclinical trials\n, which your Medical Oncologist will help identify, as well as discuss with you the benefits of having your pet participating in a trial.\nThis was the best care I have ever experienced. Everything was thoroughly explained and the care Chloe received was wonderful. We couldn’t have put our girl in better hands!\nPeople Grid Category\nof\nCare Team\nSwitch to Previous Category\n/\nSwitch to Next Category\nFaculty\nStaff Veterinarians\nResidents\nInterns\nTechnicians\nShay Bracha\nDVM, DACVIM\nAssociate Professor\nRhonda Burge\nDVM, DACVIM\nAssociate Professor - Clinical\nburge.86@osu.edu\n614-247-4722\nDah-Renn Fu\nBVM, MVM, PhD, MS, DACVR\nAssistant Professor - Clinical\nfu.977@osu.edu\n614-292-3551\nEric Green\nDVM, DACVR\nProfessor - Clinical; Diagnostic Imaging Section Head; Excellence in Veterinary Care Diagnostic Imaging Professorship\ngreen.689@osu.edu\n(614) 292-1040\nBrian Husbands\nDVM, DACVIM\nProfessor - Clinical; Vice Chair of Small Animal Faculty Success; Integrated Oncology Section Head\nhusbands.2@osu.edu\n614-292-3551\nWilliam Kisseberth\nDVM, MS, PhD, DACVIM\nProfessor\nkisseberth.2@osu.edu\n(614) 292-3551\nHunter Piegols\nDVM, DACVS-SA, ACVS Fellow-Surgical Oncology\nAssistant Professor\nLaura Selmic\nBVetMed (Hons), MPH, DACVS-SA, DECVS, ACVS Founding Fellow, Surgical Oncology, ACVS Founding Fellow, Maxillofacial and Oral Surgery\nProfessor; Teckie and Don Shackelford Chair in Canine Medicine\nselmic.1@osu.edu\n614-292-3551\nElaina Davis\nResident, Medical Oncology, 2025-2028\ndavis.7791@osu.edu\n614-292-7937\nSamantha Dowell\nDVM\nResident, Medical Oncology 2025-2028\ndowell.91@osu.edu\nJeilene Hambly\nDVM\nResident, Medical Oncology 2023-2026\nKathryn Jensen\nDVM\nResident, Medical Oncology 2024-2027\nHannah Robertson\nDVM\nResident, Medical Oncology 2024-2027\nRachel Wong\nDVM\nResident, Medical Oncology 2023-2026\nAriel Osburn\nRVT\nTechnician\nBrian Skock\nRVT\nService Coordinator\nClinical Trials\nThe Medical Oncology service is often recruiting patients for a number of studies for which your pet may be eligible. If you have any questions regarding your pet's eligibility, please contact the Blue Buffalo Clinical Trials Office (\ncvm-clinicaltrials@osu.edu\n).\nFor a listing of current trials please click\nhere\n.\nSupport Medical Oncology\nGive to support Veterinary Medicine Oncology Services and Care\nGive to support Veterinary Medicine Oncology Research Breakthroughs\nThe Ohio State University\nVeterinary Medical Center Facebook Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Instagram Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Twitter Page\nVeterinary Medical Center LinkedIn Page\nVeterinary Medical Center YouTube Page\nVeterinary Medical Center at Dublin\n5020 Bradenton Avenue\nDublin 43017 OH\n(614) 889-8070\nFrank Stanton Veterinary Spectrum of Care Clinic\n655 Vernon L. Tharp St\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-1573\nGalbreath Equine Center & Ralph Rogan Equine Performance Evaluation Arena\n685 Vernon L. Tharp Street\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-6661\nHospital for Farm Animals\n601 Vernon L. Tharp St\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-6661\nHummel Trueman Hospital for Companion Animals\n601 Vernon L. Tharp Street\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-3551\nLarge Animal Services at Marysville\n16410 County Home Rd\nMarysville 43040 OH\n(937) 642-2936\nHelpful Links\nCareers\nContact Us\nPay My Bill\nReferring Vets Portal\nVeterinary Medical Center Facebook Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Instagram Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Twitter Page\nVeterinary Medical Center LinkedIn Page\nVeterinary Medical Center YouTube Page\nLooking for the College of Veterinary Medicine?\nPlease Visit\nvet.osu.edu\nPlease Call\n(614) 292-1171\nNon-discrimination Notice\nPrivacy Statement\nCookie Settings\n©\n2026\nThe Ohio State University\nIf you have a disability and experience difficulty accessing this content, contact\nCVM-DigitalAccessibility@osu.edu",
